      "message": "I encountered a bpfloader-failed problem on some GSI images due to a missing bpf_create_map (xsk_port_map) [1]. These BPF programs require CONFIG_XDP_SOCKETS\u003dy to run properly. I encountered a compilation failure [2] when setting this config in kona-perf_defconfig. After merging this patch, I was able to compile successfully and start the Android system normally.\n\n```\n[1]:\n../net/xdp/xdp_umem.c:54:22: error: no member named \u0027umem\u0027 in \u0027struct netdev_rx_queue\u0027\n   54 |                 dev-\u003e_rx[queue_id].umem \u003d umem;\n      |                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ^\n../net/xdp/xdp_umem.c:56:22: error: no member named \u0027umem\u0027 in \u0027struct netdev_queue\u0027\n   56 |                 dev-\u003e_tx[queue_id].umem \u003d umem;\n      |                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ^\n../net/xdp/xdp_umem.c:63:29: error: no member named \u0027umem\u0027 in \u0027struct netdev_rx_queue\u0027\n   63 |                 return dev-\u003e_rx[queue_id].umem;\n      |                        ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ^\n../net/xdp/xdp_umem.c:65:29: error: no member named \u0027umem\u0027 in \u0027struct netdev_queue\u0027\n   65 |                 return dev-\u003e_tx[queue_id].umem;\n      |                        ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ^\n../net/xdp/xdp_umem.c:76:22: error: no member named \u0027umem\u0027 in \u0027struct netdev_rx_queue\u0027\n   76 |                 dev-\u003e_rx[queue_id].umem \u003d NULL;\n      |                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ^\n../net/xdp/xdp_umem.c:78:22: error: no member named \u0027umem\u0027 in \u0027struct netdev_queue\u0027\n   78 |                 dev-\u003e_tx[queue_id].umem \u003d NULL;\n      |                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ^\n6 errors generated.\nmake[3]: *** [../scripts/Makefile.build:338：net/xdp/xdp_umem.o] 错误 1\nmake[2]: *** [../scripts/Makefile.build:642：net/xdp] 错误 2\nmake[2]: *** 正在等待未完成的任务....\n```\n\n```\n[2]:\n\u003c15\u003e[    5.590299] NetBpfLoad: Loading ELF object /apex/com.android.t